 ## Clean context — the round starts empty
 
 Context comes only from your own context stages: scope, the Review Context Pack, the memory stage and the layers. Your session memory, the auto-memory index (`MEMORY.md`), remembered feedback and the earlier conversation are not inputs: do not read, quote or apply them.
 - **Accepted exceptions, the only three:** `prior_findings` of an earlier round of the same package; review-notes and learning that reach you through the memory stage; a reviewer's own `memory_search`.
 - **One memory read.** Run the stage query once and record it with `keryx review start … --memory-query "<query>"`. keryx writes `<package>/tool-calls/orchestrator.jsonl` itself from the moment the package starts: never create, edit or append to it. Readiness item 10, `memory-outside-stage`, blocks `review complete` and `review publish` on any other memory call; only the operator's waiver lifts it: in keryx shell call `review_waive_readiness` (a card, never a terminal), outside it `--waive memory-outside-stage "<operator quote>"` in a terminal; unattended, record it as Not run. Detail: `SKILL.detail.md` § "Clean context".

